## TL;DR — 60-Second Answer

**5 reasons lab wins under $5K for a marquise diamond:**

1. **Price gap is 84% at 1ct** — natural 1ct G VS2 costs $4,607; lab 1ct D VVS2 costs $657
2. **The Carat Jump** — $5K buys a 1ct natural or a 2ct+ lab D VVS1 ($2,403); that's double the stone
3. **Zero visible difference** — lab and natural marquise are identical face-up, physically, and chemically
4. **Grade upgrade** — $5K lab budget buys D VVS1; $5K natural budget buys H VS2
5. **Resale matters less under $5K** — natural recovers 40–50% at resale; lab 10–20%; but under $5K, the $3,000+ you save buying lab is the real hedge

**The clearest example from certified market inventory:**
- [1ct H VS2 natural GIA — $4,393](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30259333?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- [2ct D VVS1 lab IGI — $2,403](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29029139?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- Same budget. Lab gives you twice the marquise.

→ Browse natural marquise: [GIA Certified Marquise](https://www.bluenile.com/diamonds?Shape=marquise-cut&CertificateToggle=yes&Lab=GIA&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
→ Browse lab marquise: [IGI Certified Lab Marquise](https://www.bluenile.com/diamonds/lab-grown-diamonds?Shape=marquise-cut&CertificateToggle=yes&Lab=GIA,IGI,GCAL&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

