## Frequently Asked Questions

### Is a lab marquise diamond as good as a natural one?

Yes, physically and chemically. A [lab-grown marquise diamond](/lab-grown-marquise-diamond) is identical to a natural in hardness (10 Mohs), fire, brilliance, and crystal structure. The only difference is origin. Natural formed underground over billions of years. Lab grew in a controlled environment in weeks. You cannot tell them apart by looking. You need a spectroscope or a lab instrument.

### How much cheaper is a lab marquise than a natural one?

At 1ct, lab is 84% cheaper. A natural 1ct G VS2 GIA marquise costs $4,607. A lab 1ct D VVS2 IGI marquise costs $657. The gap is similar across all carat tiers. At 0.75ct, lab D VS1 at $455 vs natural G VS1 at $1,888 — a 76% difference.

### What does the same budget get me: natural vs lab marquise?

At $5,000, natural gets you a 1ct H VS2 GIA at $4,393. Lab gets you a 2ct D VVS1 IGI at $2,403. Double the size. Top color. Near-top clarity. $1,600 remaining. At $2,000, natural buys 0.75ct H VS1. Lab buys 1.5ct D VVS1. The Carat Jump is real at every tier.

### Does a lab marquise hold its value?

No — not well. Lab marquise diamonds recover 10–20% of retail at resale. Natural marquise recover 40–50%. Lab diamond prices have fallen 40–70% in five years. New lab stones compete against older ones at lower prices. If resale matters, buy natural. If size and grade matter more, buy lab. See our [marquise diamond resale value guide](/marquise-diamond-resale-value) for full data.

### Should I buy a natural or lab marquise for an engagement ring?

Under $5K, lab. You get a larger stone with better grades. Over $5K with long-term value in mind, natural. A GIA natural [marquise engagement ring](/marquise-diamond-engagement-ring) stone holds 40–50% resale. And it has a geological origin that lab cannot replicate. Under $5K, the savings and size advantage of lab outweigh the resale difference.

### What certification should a lab marquise diamond have?

IGI is the standard certification for lab-grown marquise diamonds. It's accepted by all major retailers. GIA also certifies lab-grown diamonds. GIA lab certs are slightly harder to find and cost a small premium. GCAL is also accepted. Avoid uncertified lab stones regardless of the seller's claims.

### Do lab marquise diamonds have the same cut quality as natural?

Yes. A well-cut lab marquise follows the same proportion targets as natural: depth 58–62%, table 53–63%, L/W ratio 1.85–2.00:1. IGI certificates for lab marquise include a Cut grade (Excellent, Ideal, Very Good). [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/) does not grade Cut for marquise of any origin — only Polish and Symmetry.

### What is the bowtie effect in a marquise diamond — does it affect natural and lab equally?

Yes. The bowtie is a dark shadow across the center belly of a marquise. It's a function of cut geometry, not origin. Both natural and lab marquise can show bowtie. It's minimized by proper depth and pavilion angles. A well-cut lab marquise has less bowtie than a poorly-cut natural. Origin doesn't affect bowtie; cut does.

### At what budget does natural become the better choice over lab?

Around $5,000–$7,000 for buyers who care about resale. Below $5K, the Carat Jump and savings make lab the clear winner. Above $7K, a natural GIA marquise holds enough resale value to justify the premium. Especially at 1.25ct+. At 1.5ct+, natural is the better long-term choice if you ever plan to sell.

### Can you tell a lab marquise from a natural marquise in a ring?

No. Once set in a [marquise diamond ring](/marquise-diamond-ring) or [marquise diamond necklace](/marquise-diamond-necklace), lab and natural marquise are visually identical. The fire, brilliance, and elongated shape look the same. A gemologist needs a spectroscope to distinguish them even from a loose stone. Friends, family, and casual observers cannot tell.

### How do I find a GIA-certified natural marquise diamond?

Use the shape and cert filter: [Browse GIA Certified Natural Marquise](https://www.bluenile.com/diamonds?Shape=marquise-cut&CertificateToggle=yes&Lab=GIA&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Every stone links to the official GIA report. Check the four cert fields: Color (G-H), Clarity (VS2), Measurements (L/W 1.85–2.00:1), Depth/Table % (58–62% / 53–63%).

### How do I find an IGI-certified lab marquise diamond?

Use the lab-grown section with cert filter: [Browse IGI Certified Lab Marquise](https://www.bluenile.com/diamonds/lab-grown-diamonds?Shape=marquise-cut&CertificateToggle=yes&Lab=GIA,IGI,GCAL&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Apply the same proportion checks as natural. IGI grades Cut for marquise. Filter for Excellent or Ideal cut alongside your target color and clarity.

### Is a 2ct lab marquise worth more than a 1ct natural marquise?

Face-up: yes, the 2ct lab is larger and more impressive. Financially: the 1ct natural holds more resale value. A 2ct D VVS1 lab at $2,403 will resell for $240–$480. A 1ct H VS2 natural GIA at $4,393 will resell for $1,757–$2,197. If the ring is for wearing, the 2ct lab wins. If it's partly an investment, the 1ct natural wins.
